[{"id":"VRCE-2-51-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":51,"verse":1,"english":"Having for a long time conversed with Sumantra, Guha distressed at heart on Rāma reaching the southern bank, retraced his steps homewards.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-57-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2051001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0bb6b36853f3e86286ec6b432f08348d04bcc966dc0250b1e1e84d27c1c3b895","compact":"f7f25be7c15ce75270df755e499fff2a486a6b7b3fa4e6dcfbb7ee1893f96fa8","nasal":"2ccf512df65d55570c58d077cf312d761b70d12c98f92bb82cfc8f9441a6acb0"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-51-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":51,"verse":2,"english":"Learning from envoys at (Śrngaverapura) all about Rāma's visit to Bharadvāja at Prayāga and his reception (at Bharadvāja's place) as well as their destined journey (to Citrakuta), Sumantra, taking the permission (of Guha), yoked those excellent horses and with a heavy heart directed his course to the city of Ayodhyā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-57-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2051002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c96d0fd77b3d7284c9c83a14e3fba55dd17fc00d60baf7d6445a8d1084e9f096","compact":"44a4602a1c65bf7bf5c6f6f7df7ef21d434f8f4e92e80751c8ca271aa6bd49ac","nasal":"7b4f499c3782eeef9b6a6e72a6839ff3d1d476cc1908bea84317b849a6441210"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-51-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":51,"verse":3,"english":"And beholding perfumed woods and rivers and watery expanses and towns and villages, he eagerly proceeded on his way.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.818,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-57-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2051003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c800800a1ed4b6dc2d5c1b346082957db917a30cc174c5a2b011b2f17584e257","compact":"5773c7ed82fd7cfaed3bd5aac23b2f2f7c5620be42a42b6212893e1fd50fff5b","nasal":"5bbce338d0880a78c1bad08aa69063de0e94a2e0da047ef0bee44a764c3641ce"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-51-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":51,"verse":4,"english":"And on the third day at dusk the charioteer arriving at Ayodhyā saw it bereft of happiness.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.842,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-57-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2051004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"517b0f26fb2fc34db0a75678f1351ec495f060ebe0e7d5bbb8765f75c801a018","compact":"9ceac4ed82753e53ac444996f483730b7fd1c4855681e93fc50c77ca88bed9a2","nasal":"82dcbe566bdfacf0572a2a629bb9444eba1714c0cfeb7a605adcedd738263412"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-51-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":51,"verse":5,"english":"And beholding it empty and still, Sumantra afflicted with exceeding sorrow, and overwhelmed with grief, thought, “Perhaps the city with her elephants and horses and men and king has been consumed by the fire of grief on account of Rāma.\"","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-57-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2051005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5f8d44858d7a23d63a5fcb546104a8bec255fb5b41795c5cbdef9fdffe32b206","compact":"19ebea2c152502f60b24b7ea5502511f5863192ba85930c728557c8e2e163b5b","nasal":"ebf5892f0216b4041d2aabf81911b20e2ced07b503f73726c4e0b899878391ab"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-51-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":51,"verse":6,"english":"And beholding it empty and still, Sumantra afflicted with exceeding sorrow, and overwhelmed with grief, thought, “Perhaps the city with her elephants and horses and men and king has been consumed by the fire of grief on account of Rāma.\"","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.551,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-57-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2051006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"de685cbbff30f5ed6c34cde9f8f15ac694354d51a343b2879ae9f0093ab652cf","compact":"6d08cb61a3daf06978fbd4b0d657feb56757de1e42d935e6a3ba27abd7c80d7b","nasal":"d384a4bea780a9e223d7b615b19fd15379920e0d3d12be8ed0ada9c4935081cd"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-51-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":51,"verse":7,"english":"Thereupon, people by hundreds and thousands rushed after the charioteer, Sumantra, asking, \"Where is Rāma?”","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.746,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-57-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2051007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e4ba1b63fd1962ab7eb3cb6fb405e5ee3545aa082463a9c62559b985528325d5","compact":"1ffb2592f528a6b645624943bce04b849c7580112b97b3139d2eadc1663bb44b","nasal":"79500cb564c412fa1d090ebf10e3c0912082652b3c97bc63c0c7565e2b989948"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-51-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":51,"verse":8,"english":"To them he replied, “Having asked Rāghava on the Gangā and being permitted by him, I have been sent away by that high-souled righteous one.\" Learning that they (Rāma and the rest) had crossed over (the Ganga), the men with tears in their eyes, sighed forth “O fie!\" and began to bewail, exclaiming, “Ah Rāma.\" And he heard crowds exclaim, Not seeing Rāma in the car, we cease to exist.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-57-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2051008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6179c936753e26